Z||000002||Rick 88||09-14-2001||09:27 PM||||This is from a Pontiac brochure for an 88 GT 5-speed with 3.61 axle ratio.<P>0-60          8.7 sec.<BR>1/4 mi.       17.1 sec.<BR>Braking, 60-0 186 ft.<BR>Lateral g's   0.86<BR>hp per lb.    20.4:1<P>87 should be similar.<P>Remember the Sunbird Turbo 2.0 5-speed?<P>0-60          7.8 sec.<BR>1/4 mi.       15.9 sec. (quick little sucker)<BR>Braking 60-0  174.9 ft.<BR>Lateral g's   0.83<BR>hp per lb.    14.6:1<P>Compare this to 88 5.7 GTA Trans Am<P>0-60          6.5 sec.<BR>1/4 m1.       15.8 sec.<BR>Braking 60-0  139 ft.<BR>Lateral g's   0.86<BR>hp per lb.    15.3:1<P>Just for your information and amusement,<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FullOutPwr||09-14-2001||09:38 PM||||THANKS! Wow.. 88 5.7 gta fast little thing.<P>------------------<BR>9-11-01 forever in our hearts<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||HummelHund||09-14-2001||09:48 PM||||I think those Pontiac numbers may be a little conservative, in most of the Car and Driver, Road and Track, and Motor Trend type reviews they were getting 7.8-8.0 sec 0-60 times.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||09-14-2001||10:39 PM||||Watched an 87GT bone stock run a 15.8 over and over. I think it's feasable to say it's a high 7 sec car to sixty and mid to high 15's in the 1/4.<P>JM||||reg||1
